The Kwai Chung Subdivided Flat Residents Alliance released the results of a survey it carried out last month on Saturday. 124 residents of inadequate housing were interviewed.

The findings show that about 80 percent of respondents reported disruptions at least once during severe weather events such as typhoons and heavy rainstorms.  The primary problems identified were water seepage and leaks, flooding, power failures and damage to appliances and furniture.

Several respondents described more extreme damage, with roofs detaching, windows shattering and ceilings caving in, endangering personal safety and forcing some to escape.

The alliance has urged enhanced assistance for those in need.  Kailey Ng, a member of the group, said, “Respondents have experienced significant disruptions in their daily lives and surroundings due to extreme weather conditions.”
