A potential train disaster on the Milan‑Lecco railway was narrowly avoided on Wednesday when a sinkhole emerged along the tracks near Bulciago station in Lecco province. Firefighters were able to stop a locomotive just metres from the collapsed section, preventing a derailment.

The sinkhole caused the earth to collapse beneath a segment of railway track, forcing a temporary halt to line operations. The incident is part of a broader wave of severe weather that has battered Italy since Tuesday, producing flooding, landslides and toppled trees across several regions.

