The total economic impact was estimated at 193 million Barbados dollars, equivalent to 0.15 % of the nation’s GDP. Of the overall effects, damage accounted for 58 %, losses for 36 %, and additional expenses for 5 %. Tourism, fisheries, agriculture, and the environment together represented 84 % of these impacts.

