Munich Re, a leading German reinsurance company, announced on Tuesday that the wildfires that swept the Los Angeles area in January caused about $40 billion in insured losses, the largest natural‑disaster loss for the insurer since the 2011 Fukushima disaster. The blazes killed 31 people and destroyed more than 16,000 homes and other structures in Los Angeles. Munich Re said nearly 90 percent of the total losses were weather‑related.

