On Boxing Day, Alberta’s two largest cities—Calgary and Edmonton—were placed under blowing‑snow advisories. Environment Canada said the advisories were issued because wind and precipitation were reducing visibility to near‑zero, making travel hazardous. Wind chills were expected to approach –35 °C, with some areas experiencing perceived temperatures as low as –37 °C.

